# Frontend React/TypeScript Conventions

## Component Structure

```
frontend/src/
  components/     # Reusable UI components
    ui/           # Primitives (Button, Input, Modal, Avatar)
    layout/       # Sidebar, Header, MainLayout
  features/       # Feature-specific components grouped by domain
    auth/         # LoginForm, RegisterForm
    guild/        # GuildList, GuildSettings
    channel/      # ChannelList, ChannelHeader
    message/      # MessageList, MessageInput, MessageItem
    voice/        # VoicePanel, VoiceControls
  hooks/          # Custom hooks
  stores/         # Zustand stores
  lib/            # API client, WS client, utils
  types/          # Shared TypeScript types
  pages/          # Route-level page components
```

## Component Pattern

```tsx
interface GuildListProps {
  onSelect: (guildId: string) => void;
}

export function GuildList({ onSelect }: GuildListProps) {
  const guilds = useGuildStore((s) => s.guilds);

  return (
    <div className="guild-list">
      {guilds.map((g) => (
        <GuildIcon key={g.id} guild={g} onClick={() => onSelect(g.id)} />
      ))}
    </div>
  );
}
```

Rules:
- Named exports only (no default exports)
- Function declarations, not arrow const
- Props interface defined directly above the component
- Destructure props in the parameter

## Zustand Store Pattern

```tsx
interface AuthStore {
  user: User | null;
  token: string | null;
  login: (email: string, password: string) => Promise<void>;
  logout: () => void;
}

export const useAuthStore = create<AuthStore>((set) => ({
  user: null,
  token: null,
  login: async (email, password) => {
    const { data } = await api.post("/auth/login", { email, password });
    set({ user: data.user, token: data.accessToken });
  },
  logout: () => {
    set({ user: null, token: null });
  },
}));
```

## API Client

Use a centralized axios instance in `lib/api.ts` with interceptors for auth token injection and refresh.

## Styling

Use Tailwind CSS utility classes. Extract repeated patterns into component-level classes via `@apply` only when used 3+ times.

## Types

Shared types go in `types/`. API response types mirror the backend `Response` envelope:

```tsx
interface ApiResponse<T> {
  data?: T;
  error?: string;
}
```
